{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game","id":1004452,"title":"Need Help with Combat W20 Mixed Breed Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T08:55:16-08:00","id":1004452,"title":"Need Help with Combat W20 Mixed Breed Game","content":"So, after reading a few suggestions from various older forums I ended up just getting confused so I thought it might be best to make a new thread on my specific situation.<br /> <br /> Some background:<br /> So managed to get our D&amp;D, Fates, GURP group to play WTA with me as the DM/ST. Despite me being completely new to Tablrletop RPGs. With the condition that they play anything but a Garou. So I have a group that consits of Bastete/Homid/Khan, a Kitsune/Shinju/Doshi and a Nagah/Vasuki/Kali with access to some Wendigo-ish gifts, a Rank system and their tribe weakness. With the expection of one whose really into his character (the Nagah). Most weren't too thrilled with the game mainly because of the combat system. They are the system mastery, gotta get the best stuff, combat heavy kind of players since they play mostly D&amp;D and Fates. I know the mechanical system is kinda clunky so I was wondering if anyone had any advice that might help make combat more interesting for these players? <br /> Thanks a bunch!<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Oh! And another question that might seem a bit dumb. My Khan and Kitsune player noticed that their weapons were actually weaker then their character's claws/bite is that normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","user":"Story","date":". 11-17-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:50:36-08:00","id":1004484,"title":"","content":"You're doing the Nagah wrong if they're in a tribe. Now, I do hate the concept of super secret splats, but if you want chilly Gifts, you just play a Kali Aspect Nagah (which the character is already, so great), not one with inroads to a tribal totem that only accepts Garou as a member of their tribe, and if you want a Nagah with a coherent Renown and Rank system,. play in the Beast Courts. This should be simple, since you're playing with a Kitsune and their internal culture is such that they think of themselves as members of the courts first and a distinct breed second. The Khan is easy to work in, as well.<br /> <br /> Regarding combat, if you just want to cut out rolling, you could use the concept of defensive values from Exalted, where you just take half the dice pool that a defensive dice pool would be and set it as the difficulty to hit. As an upshot, if you do it the way that EX3 does it, it means that you can hit with 0 net successes and just deal base damage, making the addition of attack successes to damage a bit more organic.<br /> <br /> System mastery as a concept is something you might have to wean them off of. Combat is not the only thing that they'll be doing. Focusing only on combat, in fact, is what got the world into its present mess, typically by way of Garou rampages. They're going to have to exercise other capacities to meet their actual goals, and having high Rage is going to make that difficult. Mostly for the Khan, since the Nagah and Kitsune typically have lower values (and it's twice as expensive for Nagah to buy, while Kitsune under its influence will only run away, never sticking around to tear shit up).<br /> <br /> As for their natural weapons, yes, that's working as intended. They're mighty beings of wrath meant to defeat the troubles and foes of the world, to whom violence comes easily, and they don't need swords or guns to wreck shit. Put another way, think about what monsters can do in a monster movie. They can typically move through obstacles like a miniature kaiju; in fact, Mokole can turn into kaiju-sized monsters in Archid, thanks to the doubling rate of the Tall and Behemoth traits, which the system cannot handle with the stats given. I typically think that at that point, you have to start using the demolition rules from Hunter Book: Avenger, but I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:20:08-08:00","id":1004508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004484#post1004484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're doing the Nagah wrong if they're in a tribe. Now, I do hate the concept of super secret splats, but if you want chilly Gifts, you just play a Kali Aspect Nagah (which the character is already, so great), not one with inroads to a tribal totem that only accepts Garou as a member of their tribe, and if you want a Nagah with a coherent Renown and Rank system,. play in the Beast Courts. This should be simple, since you're playing with a Kitsune and their internal culture is such that they think of themselves as members of the courts first and a distinct breed second. The Khan is easy to work in, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know the Nagah is utterly loopsy. It's a long story but basically my players picked out what they thought looked the coolest without actually reading what each breed was all about (again as long as it wasn't Garou because they don't like werewolves) I let them do it because I wanted them to play. That was rookie mistake on my part because I already had a story planned out and it wasn't set in the Beast Courts as I hadnt read the book yet and wanted a western setting with social ideas I was more familiar with (having read the Corebook and the old supplements like Rage Across Appalachias and New York) so I choose a western setting and brought the players characters there. The Kitsune is from the east though (Japan), the Khan is from the US and is a lost cub, while the Nagah has been everywhere but has lived with the Wendigo in Canada and is a lost cub too (I'm sorry if that just made your head explode because it is absurd). For the Nagah, I added that Rank system so everyone was on the same page as it were.<br /> Now, that I have read the book, that is a good point and missed opportunity. I'm going to ask the players if they want change of setting...But Just to you know what why things are the way they are for the Nagah.<br /> <br /> I respond to your other points in just a sec.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:17:42-08:00","id":1004537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004484#post1004484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding combat, if you just want to cut out rolling, you could use the concept of defensive values from Exalted, where you just take half the dice pool that a defensive dice pool would be and set it as the difficulty to hit. As an upshot, if you do it the way that EX3 does it, it means that you can hit with 0 net successes and just deal base damage, making the addition of attack successes to damage a bit more organic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, so if I understand right it cuts out the soaking roll? That seems like a good idea to make the combat less tedious. I'll be honest, I've never read Exaulted before so I'll take a quick look at its system and see if I like that better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System mastery as a concept is something you might have to wean them off of. Combat is not the only thing that they'll be doing. Focusing only on combat, in fact, is what got the world into its present mess, typically by way of Garou rampages. They're going to have to exercise other capacities to meet their actual goals, and having high Rage is going to make that difficult. Mostly for the Khan, since the Nagah and Kitsune typically have lower values (and it's twice as expensive for Nagah to buy, while Kitsune under its influence will only run away, never sticking around to tear shit up). </div> </div> </div>Yeah you're right, though it might be hard. The first thing my group did when they found out a Garou survived a bullet to the head was to find silver bullets and get around the silver weakness of the Khan. It was interesting. <br /> Though I don't want to make my game very combat focused if possible. I just want to make it fun for them when it eventually does happen and make those fights have meaning when it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for their natural weapons, yes, that's working as intended. They're mighty beings of wrath meant to defeat the troubles and foes of the world, to whom violence comes easily, and they don't need swords or guns to wreck shit. Put another way, think about what monsters can do in a monster movie. They can typically move through obstacles like a miniature kaiju; in fact, Mokole can turn into kaiju-sized monsters in Archid, thanks to the doubling rate of the Tall and Behemoth traits, which the system cannot handle with the stats given. I typically think that at that point, you have to start using the demolition rules from Hunter Book: Avenger, but I digress. </div> </div> </div>Okay great! I thought I should ask that then before they convinced me to give them Overpowered weapons earily on (which they almost did).<br /> Pfft...I told them they should have been a Mokole, they sound like crazy fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12036-story","name":"Story","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:31:59-08:00","id":1004631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004508#post1004508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, that I have read the book, that is a good point and missed opportunity. I'm going to ask the players if they want change of setting...But Just to you know what why things are the way they are for the Nagah.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is your game, and you are already deviating form the book, so you could always just set up an Beast Court like system wherever you have your game taking place. That could give your players a reason to work together since they should be part of the same alliance, and it would rewrite the Nagah story, which you already seem to be doing anyways.<br /> <br /> For combat rolls, you can put the rolls (to hit and damage) on the attackers side, and just half the dice pool of the defender and use that as a static defense, for both dodge and soak (rounding up). There are pluses and minuses to doing it this way, but it does severely cut down on dice rolling, which I've seen be a big problem for some (especially newer) players. This will also seem a more familiar format for players used to D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> So the way I'm proposing it you could have Joe the Garou in Crinos (Dex 4, Brawl 3) attacking Sarah the Gurahl in Crinos (Dex 2, Athletics 3). So Sarah's dodge defense is 3. Joe would roll his 7 dice and need 3 successes to hit. Additional successes add to the damage pool (Str+2 Claw, so let's say 9 dice). If Joe got 4 successes to hit, he would roll 10 dice of damage. The Gurahl (Stamina 8 in Crinos) has a 4 Soak rating, so Joe needs to roll at least that much to get damage through.<br /> <br /> I've only every played 1 game with this system, but it worked out well enough and eliminated half of the rolls.<br /> Oh, and if someone does use their action defensively then I would just double their score (to their full dice pool). Multiple actions complicate everything like they always do in the WoD system, and so I would drop the defense rating for each additional attack the defender had to deal with. You can drop it by a set amount (2?) or just half it each time. Soak pools though, stayed the same unless a maneuver like Fur Gnarl was involved, but that might be overcomplicating the idea for the moment.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:50:58-08:00","id":1004650,"title":"","content":"Actually, soak would just have its whole value automatically subtracted from pre-roll damage, at least if you're going the Aeonverse and Exalted route. You then roll a smaller number of damage dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:15:14-08:00","id":1004670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004650#post1004650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, soak would just have its whole value automatically subtracted from pre-roll damage, at least if you're going the Aeonverse and Exalted route. You then roll a smaller number of damage dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was just going over a modified system as I've used it. I wasn't quoting from a different game's combat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:08:24-08:00","id":1004774,"title":"","content":"It is a challenge coming from other systems to the St system, but honestly my players tend to like the clunky defense of rolling stamina for soak. The primary reason being they feel like they control their own fate. If you want to change then I strongly recommend going the soak subtracts directly from the damage pool ala Aeonverse and Exalted. Combat in Aeonverse games tends to be fast and brutal. Claws and fangs should be the most effective weapon in any Fera's arsenal. Bite is lower difficulty than just about every weapon around, and when added to the bite modifier in Chatro form for the Khan you will see why the Bastet prefer this form for combat.<br /> <br /> This is your game change whatever you need to change to have fun. Good Luck and Have Fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:00:36-08:00","id":1004918,"title":"","content":"As an idea, to give both sides (offense and defense) dice to roll, you could use a static defense pool (half Dex+Athletics) for the attacker to overcome. And then have the damage pool be static (Half damage pool +1 per additional success to hit) and have the victim roll soak.<br /> <br /> I think removing to soak automatically from the damage pool could/would make some higher soak enemies just impossible to hurt, if you can never get a damage pool going. (Crinos Gaoru with Luna's Armor). Then again, that could be the intent of the system.<br /> <br /> Deciding how to set up defenses and what variation of the system you go with will have some longer reaching consequences for how the game runs. Especially if you have players who are interested in doing their best to break the system in their favor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:26:53-08:00","id":1004926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004918#post1004918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an idea, to give both sides (offense and defense) dice to roll, you could use a static defense pool (half Dex+Athletics) for the attacker to overcome. And then have the damage pool be static (Half damage pool +1 per additional success to hit) and have the victim roll soak.<br /> <br /> I think removing to soak automatically from the damage pool could/would make some higher soak enemies just impossible to hurt, if you can never get a damage pool going. (Crinos Gaoru with Luna's Armor). Then again, that could be the intent of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted had minimum damage for that; unless an effect said otherwise, you got to roll at least one die of damage, even if soak reduced it to nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T09:12:20-08:00","id":1004975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004926#post1004926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted had minimum damage for that; unless an effect said otherwise, you got to roll at least one die of damage, even if soak reduced it to nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So now being sarcastic, this is an actual question: does that mean no matter how tough something is, outside of special powers, it always has a chance of taking 1 damage from an attack? With a 7 health level system, that seems a bit odd imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:38:57-08:00","id":1005022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004452-need-help-with-combat-w20-mixed-breed-game?p=1004975#post1004975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So now being sarcastic, this is an actual question: does that mean no matter how tough something is, outside of special powers, it always has a chance of taking 1 damage from an attack? With a 7 health level system, that seems a bit odd imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>One die, or possibly more if you're using a weapon with the Overwhelming tag (in 2.5e, grand daiklaves, as weapons on par with Guts's Dragonslayer, did a minimum of four dice of damage). If you are playing in a system with no allowance for additional health levels, it'd probably be better to keep the minimum damage lower, though; the higher values tended to be rather beyond what you'd find in a modern setting, anyway.<br /> <br /> Conversely, hardness, as an effect, might come into play, so that really low pre-soak damage attacks end up being turned aside completely. Usually, hardness is the province of magical armor, but vehicles and inanimate objects had it rated at their armor value, so when the Modern Era shard came out, damaging a main battle tank was a bit more difficult than just firing something weak a bunch of times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:03:32-08:00","id":1005092,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the explanation. Personally I don't think I like that as a system, but I guess I can see why it's in place. I don't know that there will ever be a perfect solution to reducing dice rolls in the WoD. Just varying degrees of &quot;better&quot;, which is in and of itself entirely subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}